# mount.ntfs (ntfs-3g) runs in vold's domain and does the same walk through the mount
# table as fsck.ntfs, down to the block device behind each mount, to make sure the card
# is not mounted already. vold may stat userdata's and no other; these are the rest of
# what is mounted here (system, cache, persist, and the modem and dsp partitions, which
# carry the generic label). NTFS cards mount regardless, so the denials are silenced.
dontaudit vold {
    block_device
    cache_block_device
    persist_block_device
    system_block_device
}:blk_file getattr;

# The periodic trim (and the one right after a first boot) goes through every writable
# ext4 mount in the fstab, /dsp among them: 16 MB of DSP firmware that nothing writes
# to. vold is refused there and trims the rest; the refusal is not worth a line in the
# log each time.
dontaudit vold adsprpcd_file:dir read;
